								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14152#msg14152"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14152#msg14152">Re: And so it begins...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #19 on:</b> February 02, 2005, 11:23:43 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I don&#039;t mind them picking the story line up, but it&#039;s totally out of the blue. I am actually really suprized that they chose FV as the plot to pick back up, heard alot of rumors about picking up the end of the Velious storyline. <br /><br />MM and Paw were just NPC model changes, with level&#039;s increased, same pathing problems still exsist, because they really did not revamp the zones. <br /><br />Also another big complaint was they kept all the old clunky graphics, and did not change any of the envrionment (IE backgrounds and such) so you have some nice looking up to date avatar models wandering around.<br /><br />And the storylines that went with it, and any quests are half baked from what I&#039;ve heard from friends.<br /><br />Basically, they just made another grind zone, with still shitty pathing.
						</td>
					</tr>
